{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And HaShem will be to me for Elohim.</b> And until now He is not for Elohim, heaven forbid. And Rashi, may his memory be for a blessing, explained that no disqualification will be found in my seed, and I do not know where this matter is alluded to in His saying ״וְהָיָה״ etc. Furthermore, this promise is always dependent and standing, and when will there be an end of the boundary to make the stone a monument? And the correct interpretation is that he intended to say that the name HaShem will be singled out to him for Elohim, in the manner that it was singled out upon his fathers (Genesis 28:13): ״אֱלֹהֵי אַבְרָהָם אֱלֹהֵי יִצְחָק״ — so too it will be said of him ״אֱלֹהֵי יַעֲקֹב״, and that is His saying <b>to me for Elohim</b>, meaning: to me in singling-out. And a great thing Jacob spoke in this, and you will find that it was indeed so, as it is written (Genesis 33:20): ״וַיִּקְרָא לוֹ אֵל אֱלֹהֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל״, and afterward he fulfilled his vow that he had vowed to make this stone."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:44:22.638028292Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}